From fc081cdfc6b370f6b6853cdeb4313f92561770d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amadeusz Sławiński <amade@asmblr.net>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:06:05 +0200
Subject: ASoC: soc-ac97: Fix error handling in snd_soc_new_ac97_component()
Mime-version: 1.0
Content-type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-transfer-encoding: 8bit
Git-commit: fc081cdfc6b370f6b6853cdeb4313f92561770d1
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

If call to snd_soc_ac97_init_gpio() fails, proper removal procedure
should mirror snd_soc_free_ac97_component() behaviour and call
device_del() before put_device().

Fixes: 9bf5c3d11f1f ("ASoC: ac97: add gpio chip")
Signed-off-by: Amadeusz Sławiński <amade@asmblr.net>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261014200608.118770-6-amade@asmblr.net
Signed-off-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 sound/soc/soc-ac97.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/soc-ac97.c b/sound/soc/soc-ac97.c
index 5f81e3606655..5c573c8dc249 100644
--- a/sound/soc/soc-ac97.c
+++ b/sound/soc/soc-ac97.c
@@ -241,10 +241,12 @@ struct snd_ac97 *snd_soc_new_ac97_component(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 
 	ret = snd_soc_ac97_init_gpio(ac97, component);
 	if (ret)
-		goto err_put_device;
+		goto err_del_device;
 
 	return ac97;
 
+err_del_device:
+	device_del(&ac97->dev);
 err_put_device:
 	put_device(&ac97->dev);
 	return ERR_PTR(ret);
-- 
